quiet.md #20: decode images only once they are visible

ImageCache gets a `peek` that reads a cached result without starting a load
or counting as a use, and Img::load_visible_only defers decoding an image with
explicit width and height until it is painted inside the visible area (layout
reads the cache through `peek` only). Images outside a card's clip are no
longer decoded up front; pixels, sizes and animation are unchanged.

